    "content": "The Ministry of Transport and Aviation of Galmudug has announced that all airports under its administration will be closed effective September 30, 2026. In an official letter addressed to the Somali Civil Aviation Authority and airline associations, the ministry cited the prevailing security situation and the electoral process taking place in the region as reasons for the shutdown.\n\nThe directive suspends all flights and related services at Galmudug's airports. It remains unclear how long the closure will remain in effect, as the ministry did not specify an end date. The move is expected to disrupt air travel between several towns in Galmudug and the capital, Mogadishu.\n\nGalmudug, a federal member state in central Somalia, has been preparing for elections in recent weeks. Security has been a persistent concern in the region, with authorities frequently adjusting measures to ensure stability during the voting period. The ministry's decision appears to be part of broader efforts to control movement and prevent potential disruptions during the electoral process.\n\nThe closure directly impacts the Somali diaspora, particularly those who travel to Galmudug for business, family visits, or to participate in the elections. Many diaspora members rely on these air links to reach their hometowns, and the suspension could complicate travel plans and delay remittance and investment activities. It may also affect humanitarian operations if aid flights are unable to land.\n\nLocal airlines and passengers now face uncertainty as they await further guidance from Galmudug authorities. The Somali Civil Aviation Authority has not yet issued a public response to the letter. Travelers are advised to check with airlines for updates on alternative routes or rescheduling.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/29/garoomada-diyaaradaha-galmudug-oo-la-xiray-doorashada-awgeed/",
